{%- comment -%}
  ElmsNest v2 PDP — §4.8 "עוד שלושה שיוצרים אווירה"  ·  #env2-pdp-related  ·  the related module,
  and the shelf that carries THE product card (snippets/elmsnest-v2-pdp-card.liquid — designed once
  here, reused as the catalogue card in round 2).

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ what this section is
  Three products of the SAME PLACE, on one baseline-staggered line above a warm floor rule. Never a
  grid of equal cells (do-not §6.2, §6.14): the widths and aspects are staggered per block
  (300 / 210 / 260 at 1/1.05 · 1/1.4 · 1/.9) and there are three of them, never four.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ where every word comes from
  Nothing here is typed about a product. The card prints the product's own title, its own price
  (elmsnest-v2-price) and its own buy control (elmsnest-v2-buy); the section itself writes only the
  editorial frame, and even that is PLACE-DRIVEN: the eyebrow, the heading and the deck's first
  clause are derived from product.type, which is 1:1 with the four collections and therefore with
  the four APPROVED place pairs (BRIEF §3). A product whose type is none of the four prints the
  quiet generic frame — never an invented place and never an invented promise.

  Because all three cards come from the SAME place, the card's own place kicker would print the same
  gold line three times in one row — texture, not information (CREATIVE-07 / TYPOGRAPHER-15). The
  section says the place once, in its eyebrow and its deck, and passes kicker: 'none' to any card
  whose place is the one the buyer is already looking at. A card from another place keeps its kicker.

  The deck is graft G (§2), the best sentence written for this brief, and it is the reason this
  module can exist at all in a store with one test order: it converts the ABSENCE of proof into
  evidence of the position. No stars, no rating, no "נמכר ביותר", no counts (BRIEF §11, §6.4).

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ the heading counts, honestly
  "עוד שלושה" is only printed when three cards actually render. Two → "עוד שניים …", one → "עוד אחד
  למרפסת" (singular, so the Hebrew stays grammatical), none → the whole section prints NOTHING.
  That is what keeps this section safe on all 27 products: a product with no place collection, or a
  collection holding only itself, renders an empty string rather than a broken shelf.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ which products
  Every block may name its own product. A block that names none is auto-filled, in order, from the
  place collection (section.settings.collection, or the product's own collection whose title equals
  product.type — which is how the "מבצעים" collection can never be picked up), skipping this
  product and anything already shown. Auto-fill can be switched off.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ images, and the 14 that have none
  No image index is written here: every card resolves its photo through elmsnest-v2-pdp-image (§3.5).
  But an index resolver cannot help a product whose photographs are ALL baked-text slides, and the
  14 handles of brief/WINNING-SPEC.md §3.6 are exactly that — verified against the live CDN on
  2026-09-02: all six images of decorative-led-net-lights and of led-globe-string-lights, and all
  seven of retro-solar-path-lights-set, are cream marketing boards with Hebrew headlines, icon rows,
  a spec table, and in one case a "שלנו מול אחרים" comparison. Cream is banned (do-not §6.1), baked
  text is banned (§6.16), and a competitor claim is banned (§6.3) — so on this shelf those products
  are never auto-filled. §3.6 already ruled how they are reached instead: "They are still sold —
  reach them through the collection links", and this section always prints that link.

  A merchant may still put one on the shelf deliberately, but only together with a card_image of
  their own; without a photograph the block is skipped and the heading counts down, because there is
  no honest picture to show. That is the one rule here that overrides a merchant setting.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ no JS / reduced motion
  The section is complete without JavaScript: all three cards, their kickers, titles and prices are
  server-rendered, the single-variant card's ATC is a real POST form to routes.cart_add_url, and the
  core sets --lit:1 whenever html.env2-js is absent or reduced motion is on — so the photographs are
  lit. JS does exactly one thing, §3.3's "related — the product photographs light on arrival":
  hand the cards to the core's shared [data-lamp] observer. The mobile shelf is a native CSS
  scroll-snap row and needs no script either.

  Plumbing: elmsnest-v2-core (from layout/theme.liquid) supplies the tokens, fonts, .env2-* helpers
  and window.env2. This section renders no global; it renders elmsnest-v2-pdp-card's stylesheet once
  (css: true) before the cards, exactly as the CONTRACT requires.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the place (the four approved pairs only)
  assign env2_type = product.type | default: ''
  assign env2_place = ''
  assign env2_short = ''
  assign env2_verb = ''
  assign env2_all = ''
  if env2_type == 'תאורת שביל, עמוד וגינה'
    assign env2_place = 'שביל, מדרגות ומעברים'
    assign env2_short = 'לשביל'
    assign env2_verb = 'שמאירים את הדרך'
    assign env2_all = 'לכל תאורת השביל, העמוד והגינה'
  elsif env2_type == 'תאורת קיר'
    assign env2_place = 'כניסה, קיר וחזית'
    assign env2_short = 'לכניסה'
    assign env2_verb = 'שמאירים נקודה מסוימת'
    assign env2_all = 'לכל תאורת הקיר'
  elsif env2_type == 'גרילנדות ותאורה דקורטיבית'
    assign env2_place = 'מרפסת ופינת ישיבה'
    assign env2_short = 'למרפסת'
    assign env2_verb = 'שיוצרים אווירה'
    assign env2_all = 'לכל הגרילנדות והתאורה הדקורטיבית'
  elsif env2_type == 'ספוטים, פרוז׳קטורים ותאורה ניידת'
    assign env2_place = 'הדגשת אזור בגינה'
    assign env2_short = 'לגינה'
    assign env2_verb = 'שמאירים עץ או ערוגה'
    assign env2_all = 'לכל הספוטים, הפרוז׳קטורים והתאורה הניידת'
  endif
  if env2_short == ''
    assign env2_short = 'מהחנות'
  endif
  if env2_verb == ''
    assign env2_verb = 'מהחנות'
  endif
  if env2_all == ''
    assign env2_all = 'לכל המוצרים'
  endif

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the collection to draw from
  assign env2_col = section.settings.collection
  if env2_col == blank and env2_type != ''
    for env2_c in product.collections
      if env2_c.title == env2_type
        assign env2_col = env2_c
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  if env2_col == blank
    for env2_c in product.collections
      unless env2_c.handle == 'sale' or env2_c.handle == 'frontpage' or env2_c.handle == 'all'
        assign env2_col = env2_c
        break
      endunless
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    Handles with no photograph a CARD can show. One assign, one place. A handle listed here is never
    auto-filled onto the shelf and is never rendered from its own images; it reaches the buyer through
    the collection link at the end of the section, exactly as §3.6 rules.
    First, the 14 of brief/WINNING-SPEC.md §3.6: every frame is a cream marketing board (verified
    against the live CDN, 2026-09-02 — six of six on decorative-led-net-lights and on
    led-globe-string-lights, seven of seven on retro-solar-path-lights-set, one of them a
    comparison board headed "שלנו מול אחרים").
    Then solar-rope-string-lights: its only near-clean frame (index 2) carries an "עמידות IP65" chip
    that §3.6 removes with object-position 50% 100%. A card crops from the centre and cannot, so it is
    excluded HERE only. The homepage still uses that frame with its crop, and round 2's catalogue card
    should gain an object-position rather than inherit this exclusion.
  endcomment
  assign env2_noimg = '|retro-solar-path-lights-set|warm-solar-step-deck-lights|waterproof-solar-deck-step-lights|solar-garden-lantern-9-led|solar-garden-spotlight-52-led|solar-security-light-100-led|modern-solar-path-lights-set|solar-floodlight-ip67-remote-timer|decorative-led-net-lights|led-globe-string-lights|modern-led-bollard-light-5w-ip65|rechargeable-telescopic-camping-lantern|swaying-solar-path-lights-ip65|magnetic-rechargeable-touch-wall-light|solar-rope-string-lights|'

  assign env2_auto = section.settings.auto_fill
  assign env2_taken = '|'
  if product != blank
    assign env2_taken = env2_taken | append: product.handle | append: '|'
  endif
  for env2_b in section.blocks
    if env2_b.settings.product != blank
      assign env2_taken = env2_taken | append: env2_b.settings.product.handle | append: '|'
    endif
  endfor
  assign env2_n = 0
  assign env2_varies = false
-%}
{%- comment -%} The cards are built first so the heading can count them and never over-promise. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture env2_cards -%}
  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
    {%- assign env2_p = block.settings.product -%}
    {%- if env2_p == blank and env2_auto and env2_col != blank -%}
      {%- for env2_cand in env2_col.products limit: 30 -%}
        {%- assign env2_mark = '|' | append: env2_cand.handle | append: '|' -%}
        {%- unless env2_taken contains env2_mark or env2_noimg contains env2_mark -%}
          {%- assign env2_p = env2_cand -%}
          {%- break -%}
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      A product with no usable photograph of its own is only shown when the block carries one.
      Everything else about the block is honoured; this is the single override, and §3.6 is why.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if env2_p != blank and block.settings.card_image == blank -%}
      {%- assign env2_mark = '|' | append: env2_p.handle | append: '|' -%}
      {%- if env2_noimg contains env2_mark -%}
        {%- assign env2_p = blank -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if env2_p != blank -%}
      {%- assign env2_taken = env2_taken | append: env2_p.handle | append: '|' -%}
      {%- assign env2_n = env2_n | plus: 1 -%}
      {%- if env2_p.price_varies and env2_p.price_min != env2_p.price_max -%}
        {%- assign env2_varies = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%} same place as the product being viewed? then the section head has already said
        it, and three identical gold kickers in one row are texture, not information. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign env2_ck = '' -%}
      {%- if env2_p.type == product.type -%}{%- assign env2_ck = 'none' -%}{%- endif -%}
      <li class="env2-pdp-related__cell" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
        {%- render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-card',
              product: env2_p,
              kicker: env2_ck,
              width: block.settings.card_width,
              aspect: block.settings.card_aspect,
              image_index: block.settings.card_image_index,
              image: block.settings.card_image,
              action_label: block.settings.card_action_label -%}
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- if env2_n > 0 -%}
{%- liquid
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the frame, counted and place-driven
  assign env2_eyebrow = section.settings.eyebrow
  if env2_eyebrow == blank
    assign env2_eyebrow = '08 · עוד ' | append: env2_short
  endif

  assign env2_heading = section.settings.heading
  if env2_heading == blank
    if env2_n == 1
      assign env2_heading = 'עוד אחד ' | append: env2_short
    elsif env2_n == 2
      assign env2_heading = 'עוד שניים ' | append: env2_verb
    else
      assign env2_heading = 'עוד שלושה ' | append: env2_verb
    endif
  endif

  comment
    The deck is graft G, §4.8, and its second sentence is verbatim. Its price clause is not: §4.8
    writes "מחיר אחד לכל אחד", which is true only while every card shows ONE price. The moment a card
    prints a range (129.90-159.90) or a floor (מ-109.90) that sentence is contradicted by the row
    underneath it, and a claim the page itself disproves is exactly what BRIEF §3 forbids. So the
    clause follows the cards: one price each when that is what they show, otherwise "a price you can
    see on each" - which is the same promise, and the one the shelf actually keeps.
  endcomment
  assign env2_deck = section.settings.deck
  if env2_deck == blank
    assign env2_price_clause = 'מחיר אחד לכל אחד.'
    if env2_varies
      assign env2_price_clause = 'מחיר גלוי לכל אחד.'
    endif
    assign env2_deck = env2_price_clause | append: ' בלי כוכבים ובלי «נמכר ביותר» — אין לנו עדיין מה למדוד.'
    if env2_place != ''
      assign env2_deck = 'מאותו מקום — ' | append: env2_place | append: '. ' | append: env2_deck
    endif
  endif

  assign env2_link_url = section.settings.link_url | default: env2_col.url
  assign env2_link_label = section.settings.link_label | default: env2_all
-%}
{% render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-card', css: true %}
<section id="env2-pdp-related" data-env2-pdp-related class="env2-section env2-pdp-related" dir="rtl" style="scroll-margin-top:90px;--env2-stars:.70" aria-labelledby="env2-pdp-related-h2">
  <div class="env2-stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="env2-wrap env2-pdp-related__wrap">
    <div class="env2-pdp-related__head">
      <div class="env2-pdp-related__title">
        {%- if env2_eyebrow != blank -%}
          <p class="env2-eyebrow env2-pdp-related__eyebrow">{{ env2_eyebrow }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <h2 id="env2-pdp-related-h2" class="env2-h env2-pdp-related__h2">{{ env2_heading }}</h2>
      </div>
      {%- if env2_deck != blank -%}
        <p class="env2-pdp-related__deck">{{ env2_deck }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      The link lives INSIDE the floor, bottom-aligned with the cards. With three cards it settles into
      the space the shelf leaves at the end side; with one or two — which is what a place collection
      made mostly of never-use handles can honestly offer — it fills that space instead of leaving a
      hole, and it is the thing the buyer needs there: the rest of the place, one click away.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="env2-pdp-related__floor">
      <ul class="env2-pdp-related__row" role="list" data-env2-pdp-related-row>{{ env2_cards }}</ul>
      {%- if env2_link_url != blank and env2_link_label != blank -%}
        <p class="env2-pdp-related__after">
          <a class="env2-link env2-pdp-related__all" href="{{ env2_link_url }}">{{ env2_link_label }}
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M19 12H5M11 6l-6 6 6 6"/></svg>
          </a>
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
/* ---------- §4.8 the related shelf: head, a staggered line of cards, a warm floor rule ----------
   The card itself is styled by snippets/elmsnest-v2-pdp-card.liquid (rendered once with css: true
   above), so nothing here restyles a shared class — this file only composes the shelf. The section
   paints no background: the ground is the body gradient from elmsnest-v2-ground-product (§3.1). */
.env2-pdp-related{padding-block:100px 90px}
.env2-pdp-related__wrap{position:relative;z-index:1}

/* head: eyebrow + h2 at the start, graft G's deck at the end, bottoms aligned.
   The deck is NOT text-align:end: in RTL "end" is flush-left and ragged-right, so the rag falls on
   the side the eye returns to and the third line strands 255px inboard (TYPOGRAPHER-03). The flex
   placement already puts the paragraph at the end side; the text inside it aligns to start. */
.env2-pdp-related__head{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-end;gap:24px 40px;margin-bottom:56px}
.env2-pdp-related__title{min-width:0;flex:1 1 22ch}
.env2-pdp-related__eyebrow{margin-bottom:18px}
.env2-pdp-related__h2.env2-h{font-size:clamp(34px,4.8vw,70px);max-width:16ch}
.env2-pdp-related__deck{flex:0 1 38ch;margin:0 0 .35em;max-width:38ch;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--env2-ink-2);text-wrap:pretty}

/* the floor: one warm rule the objects stand on, bleeding past the wrap on both sides
   (.env2-section is overflow-x:clip, so the bleed can never scroll the page). The shelf and the
   collection link share it, bottom-aligned; the link wraps to its own line when they do not fit. */
.env2-pdp-related__floor{position:relative;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end;gap:28px clamp(28px,4vw,64px);padding-block-end:40px}
.env2-pdp-related__floor::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset-inline:-10vw;inset-block-end:0;block-size:1px;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent,rgba(255,211,148,.42) 28%,rgba(255,211,148,.42) 72%,transparent)}

/* the line of cards: staggered widths and aspects (never equal cells), bottoms aligned */
.env2-pdp-related__row{list-style:none;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;gap:clamp(18px,3vw,48px);margin:0;padding:0;min-width:0;flex:0 1 auto}
.env2-pdp-related__cell{flex:0 0 auto;min-width:0;margin:0;padding:0}

/* the closing link to the whole collection */
.env2-pdp-related__after{flex:1 0 auto;display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;margin:0;padding-block-end:2px}
.env2-pdp-related__all{color:var(--env2-ink-2)}

/* ---------- mobile: a scroll-snap shelf, not a squeezed line (§4.8, do-not §6.18) ----------
   The row scrolls inside itself — the negative inline margin is exactly one gutter, so the page
   itself never scrolls horizontally at 360px. Card width comes from the card snippet's own
   min(--env2-pdp-card-w, 62vw), which leaves the next card peeking as the affordance. */
@media (max-width:900px){
  .env2-pdp-related{padding-block:72px 64px}
  .env2-pdp-related__head{display:block;margin-bottom:30px}
  .env2-pdp-related__eyebrow{margin-bottom:14px}
  .env2-pdp-related__h2.env2-h{max-width:none}
  .env2-pdp-related__deck{max-width:none;margin:16px 0 0;font-size:15.5px}
  .env2-pdp-related__floor{display:block;padding-block-end:26px}
  .env2-pdp-related__row{gap:20px;overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:visible;scroll-snap-type:x mandatory;scrollbar-width:none;-ms-overflow-style:none;margin-inline:calc(-1 * var(--env2-gut));padding-inline:var(--env2-gut);padding-block-end:4px;scroll-padding-inline-start:var(--env2-gut);-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;overscroll-behavior-x:contain}
  .env2-pdp-related__row::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
  .env2-pdp-related__cell{scroll-snap-align:start}
  .env2-pdp-related__after{justify-content:flex-start;margin-block-start:26px;padding-block-end:0}
  .env2-pdp-related__all{min-height:44px}
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
/* §3.3, the related row: "the product photographs light on arrival ([data-lamp])" — and that is the
   whole job. Every card is server-rendered and buyable without this file; the core sets --lit:1
   when html.env2-js is absent or reduced motion is on, so no-JS and reduced-motion visitors get a
   fully lit, fully working shelf. Ends with the CONTRACT's env2.observe fallback line. */
(function () {
  function init(el) {
    if (el.__env2PdpRelated) return;
    el.__env2PdpRelated = true;
    window.env2 ? env2.observe(el) : el.querySelectorAll('[data-lamp]').forEach(function (l) { l.classList.add('lit'); });
  }
  function boot(root) {
    var scope = (root && root.querySelectorAll) ? root : document;
    scope.querySelectorAll('[data-env2-pdp-related]').forEach(init);
    if (scope !== document && scope.matches && scope.matches('[data-env2-pdp-related]')) init(scope);
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () { boot(document); });
  } else {
    boot(document);
  }
  document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load', function (e) { boot(e.target || document); });
})();
{% endjavascript %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "ElmsNest v2 — PDP קשורים",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "כותרת עליונה קטנה", "info": "ריק = לפי המקום של המוצר, למשל «08 · עוד למרפסת»." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "כותרת", "info": "ריק = לפי המקום ולפי מספר המוצרים שבאמת מוצגים, למשל «עוד שלושה שיוצרים אווירה»." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "deck", "label": "שורת פתיחה (בצד השני של הכותרת)", "info": "ריק = לפי המקום, ולפי המחירים שהכרטיסים באמת מציגים (מחיר אחד לכל אחד / מחיר גלוי לכל אחד), ואחריו: בלי כוכבים ובלי «נמכר ביותר» — אין לנו עדיין מה למדוד." },
    { "type": "collection", "id": "collection", "label": "קולקציה למילוי אוטומטי", "info": "ריק = הקולקציה של המקום שאליו שייך המוצר." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "auto_fill", "label": "למלא אוטומטית מוצרים חסרים מהקולקציה", "default": true, "info": "כבו כדי להציג רק את המוצרים שנבחרו ידנית." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "link_label", "label": "טקסט הקישור לקולקציה", "info": "ריק = לפי המקום, למשל «לכל הגרילנדות והתאורה הדקורטיבית»." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "link_url", "label": "יעד הקישור", "info": "ריק = עמוד הקולקציה שממנה נלקחו המוצרים." }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 3,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "card",
      "name": "מוצר",
      "limit": 3,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "product", "id": "product", "label": "מוצר", "info": "ריק = מילוי אוטומטי מהקולקציה, ללא המוצר הנוכחי." },
        { "type": "range", "id": "card_width", "label": "רוחב הכרטיס", "min": 180, "max": 360, "step": 10, "unit": "px", "default": 280, "info": "הרוחבים נבחרים שונים זה מזה בכוונה — לא שלושה תאים זהים." },
        { "type": "select", "id": "card_aspect", "label": "יחס התמונה", "default": "1/1.15",
          "options": [
            { "value": "1/1.05", "label": "כמעט ריבוע (1/1.05)" },
